-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_addincludepath_byunit.pcpp - Directive compliance: @addincludepath in
  an imported unit

  A unit has no build of its own; its @addincludepath adds to the one build
  (BNF.md sec 2). This program sets no @addincludepath itself: the unit it
  imports, dir_addincludepath_byunit_unit.pcpp, adds res\tests\libs, and the
  #include of dir_addincludepath.h below is found through it. The unit
  includes the same header in its own translation unit.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addincludepath_byunit.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addincludepath_byunit.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    dir_addincludepath_value() = 30
    dir_addincludepath_byunit_unit.FromUnit() = 31
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  Both targets print the same; the [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_addincludepath_byunit;
import dir_addincludepath_byunit_unit;

#include "dir_addincludepath.h"

begin
  println("dir_addincludepath_value() = {}", cpp("dir_addincludepath_value()"));
  println("dir_addincludepath_byunit_unit.FromUnit() = {}", dir_addincludepath_byunit_unit.FromUnit());
end.
